# .dockerignore
#
# THIS FILE IS A PROVENANCE CONTROL, NOT A BUILD OPTIMISATION.
#
# `Dockerfile` runs `COPY . .`, and the working tree deliberately contains cloned checkouts of
# third-party code under `benchmark/corpora/` (paramiko, CryptoAPI-Bench, golang.org/x/crypto).
# Those are excluded from git by .gitignore -- but .gitignore is NOT consulted by Docker. Without
# this file, `docker build` would bake another project's source code into our published image, which
# is exactly the provenance failure PROVENANCE.md exists to prevent.
#
# It also keeps scratch output and local virtualenvs out of the image, and keeps the build context
# small enough that a rebuild is fast.

# ---- third-party source: must never enter the image --------------------------------------------
benchmark/corpora/
**/corpora/
benchmark/_output/
_verify/
_out/
scratch/
tmp/

# ---- scratch output from the long-running tools --------------------------------------------------
*.report.json
indramesh_report.json
_*.txt
_*.html
st.txt
st_e.txt
*.log

# ---- secrets and credentials: refuse them unconditionally -----------------------------------------
# engine/fspolicy.py refuses to read these at scan time; the build context deserves the same rule.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
.netrc
.git-credentials
.aws/
.ssh/
credentials.json
secrets/

# ---- local Python environment and caches --------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mutation_out/

# ---- VCS and editor noise ------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- local benchmark state that is regenerated, not shipped ---------------------------------------
benchmark/_bench_state.json
*.pyc
